/* ============================================================================
   craps-first-roll.epher -- the come-out roll of craps, exact fractions

   Craps opens with a come-out roll of two dice. The shooter wins at once
   with a 7 or an 11 and loses at once with a 2, a 3 or a 12; any other
   sum sets a "point" and the game continues with further rolls. Using
   the two-dice sums of the companion script (games/two-dice-sums.epher):

     P(win now)  = P(7 or 11) = (6 + 2) / 36 = 8/36 = 2/9
     P(lose now) = P(2, 3 or 12) = (1 + 2 + 1) / 36 = 4/36 = 1/9

   The remaining 24/36 = 2/3 of come-out rolls go to a point round. The
   full game, point rounds included, is won with probability 244/495 =
   0.492929292929, so the pass line carries a house edge of about 1.41%,
   which is why the casino stays in business.

   Source: Feller, "An Introduction to Probability Theory and Its
   Applications", volume 1, chapter 3 (the 244/495 value is derived
   there). All the fractions below are exact.

   Run it from a terminal:
     Linux (deb, rpm):  epher /usr/lib/epher/scripts/probability/games/craps-first-roll.epher
     Windows:           epher "$env:LOCALAPPDATA\epher\scripts\probability\games\craps-first-roll.epher"
     macOS:             epher /Applications/epher.app/Contents/Resources/scripts/probability/games/craps-first-roll.epher
   Web/desktop:             paste the file into the entry, press Enter
   ============================================================================ */

// ---- results ----
// The immediate outcomes of the come-out roll.
print("P(7 or 11, win at once):", (6 + 2) / 36)
print("P(2, 3 or 12, lose at once):", (1 + 2 + 1) / 36)

// Every other sum (4, 5, 6, 8, 9, 10) sets the point; the three
// probabilities of the first roll exhaust the 36 outcomes.
print("P(a point is set):", 24 / 36)
print("1/9 + 2/9 + 2/3 =", 1/9 + 2/9 + 2/3)

// The full pass-line probability, point rounds included, from Feller.
print("P(pass line wins the whole game):", 244 / 495)
print("house edge, fraction of the stake:", 1 - 2 * 244/495)
// The house edge is 7/495 = 0.0141414..., about 1.41 percent of the
// stake, which in percent units is exactly 140/99.
print("house edge, percent of the stake:", 100 * (1 - 2 * 244/495))
/* ---- expected output ----
= P(7 or 11, win at once): 2/9
= P(2, 3 or 12, lose at once): 1/9
= P(a point is set): 2/3
= 1/9 + 2/9 + 2/3 = 1
= P(pass line wins the whole game): 244/495
= house edge, fraction of the stake: 7/495
= house edge, percent of the stake: 140/99
*/
